cfg_bits: 16'h0010
id_readback: play {L=0xD5D51D1D, R=0x2A2AE2E2} on hw:dsp4pcm and
  record: L = design_id, R = 0xD594<cfg_bits> for 128 frames
cdc_witness: play {L=0xCD0432B4, R=0x32FBCD4B} and record, 128 frames:
  L = {7'b0, cdc_ones_last[8:0], 7'b0, cdc_ones_max[8:0]}
  R = {0xCD04, cdc_toggles_last[8:0], frame_counter[15:9]}
  cdc_ones/toggles are per 48 kHz frame over 256 TDM8 bit periods;
  the frame counter MUST advance between two knocks or the witness
  is dead and its zeros mean nothing (S81)
ad_witness: play {L=0xAD075E2<b>, R=~L} and record, 128 frames.
  The knock's low three bits are the selector:
    <b>[1:0]  lane 0, 1 or 2   (lane 3 is NOT a knock: no
               converter on AD3, it falls through to audio)
    <b>[2]    0 = counted on bck8_sample (bck8 rising, the edge
               the DSP samples the lane on -- S84's only bank)
               1 = counted on bck8_launch (bck8 falling), added
               at S85 to measure the converter launch phase
  So <b> = 0,1,2 are S84's three knocks unchanged, and 4,5,6 are
  the same three lanes on the other edge. Six banks, all counting
  the same pass at once; one knock answers about one of them.
  L = {3'b0, bck_ratio_ok, edge, lane[1:0], ad_ones_last[8:0],
       7'b0, ad_ones_max[8:0]}
  R = {0xAD07, ad_toggles_last[8:0], frame_counter[15:9]}
  Counts are per 48 kHz frame over 256 TDM8 bit periods.
  bck_ratio_ok is 1 while every conv_fs frame since power-up has
  held exactly 256 bck8 periods -- the generator's own ratio, not
  arrival at any pin.
  The frame counter is fs8 = conv_fs, which this part GENERATES:
  it witnesses that the clock generator runs, NOT that the clock
  arrives at the AK5558 pins. It MUST advance between two knocks
  or the witness is dead and its zeros mean nothing (S81/S84).
