adopted: SHIPPING from S85 (hub ruling S84-N1). The label moved from
  7a6a4529f29c because the ad[0..2] witness is now built into every
  configuration, and because S85 put CFG_BITS into the hash (S85-11).
  THE SHIPPING LANE PATH IS UNCHANGED: i_dspa[0..2] are the same
  `net_sel[n] ? ni[n] : ad[n]` wire they have always been -- the S85
  retiming and codec-substitution arms are switches and are OFF here --
  and the S82 84.34 % D24 driven capacity row was re-taken on the
  matching driveall build (943f27966c28) to prove nothing moved.
  Area cost of the witness, measured back to back on this tree:
  521/1270 LE (41 %) without it at Fmax 68.56 MHz, 882/1270 (69 %) with
  it at 67.44 MHz. Both clear the 49.152 MHz sysclk with wide margin.
  Reproducibility, checked this session: two builds of this label differ
  in ONE line of the .svf -- the `!Device #1: ... <date>` comment the
  converter stamps -- and are byte-identical everywhere else. The
  programmed content is reproducible; the file md5 is not, so identity
  rests on the design ID read off the part, which is what the standing
  read-back rule already uses.
